  "id": "gel-electrophoresis",
  "term": "gel electrophoresis",
  "definition": "Gel electrophoresis is a laboratory method used here to assess RNA integrity by separating RNA molecules in an agarose gel. In this study, a borax-based version acted in a denaturing-like way, giving RNA separation similar to formaldehyde methods while using a simpler and safer setup.",
